course: dictionary
lesson: 13362
title: Harmfully: in a way that causes harm
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: The word harmfully comes from harm, which means hurt or damage. The ending -ly turns it into a word about how something happens. So harmfully means in a way that causes harm or damage. Look at the words around it to check.
explain: «Some cleaning chemicals can act harmfully if they are swallowed.» The sentence tells you the chemicals are dangerous to the body. Swallowing is not safe, so harmfully must mean that they can cause damage. Try your meaning in the sentence: "can act in a way that causes harm if they are swallowed" still makes sense.
explain: Do not confuse harmfully with harmful. Harmful is an adjective, so it describes a thing: "harmful chemicals". Harmfully is an adverb, so it describes how something acts: "the chemicals act harmfully".
fact: Harmfully means in a way that causes harm or damage.
fact: Harm means hurt or damage, so harmfully is about something that hurts or damages.
fact: Harmful is an adjective: «harmful chemicals». Harmfully is an adverb: «acted harmfully».
fact: Science lessons often use harmfully for chemicals that can act harmfully on the body or the environment.
fact: A good check is to swap in "in a way that causes harm" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Some cleaning chemicals can act harmfully if they are swallowed.» What does harmfully mean? | In a way that smells lovely | *In a way that causes harm | Quickly and quietly | Brightly, like a light
exercise: Mum says, «Never mix bleach with other cleaners, because they can react harmfully.» What does harmfully mean? | In a way that is quiet and slow | In a way that is free | *In a way that causes harm or damage | In a way that makes things shine
exercise: Which word is the opposite of harmfully? | Happily | Loudly | *Safely | Quickly
test: «Too much sun can affect your skin harmfully.» What does harmfully mean here? | Gently and kindly | Very warmly | *In a way that causes damage | In a way that makes you laugh
test: Which word is closest in meaning to harmfully? | Quietly | Safely | *Damagingly | Happily
exam: «Some substances may act harmfully on the environment, so scientists test them carefully.» What does harmfully mean? | In a way that is very bright | *In a way that causes harm to the environment | Slowly, over many years | Helpfully, to help plants grow
